WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.240
There is a file on the internet right now that says what every hospital in Sacramento gets paid.

2
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.030
By each health plan.

3
00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:08.340
For each procedure.

4
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.030
To the cent.

5
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.460
It is public.

6
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.470
It is legal to read.

7
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.520
Almost no human being has ever read it.

8
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:15.870
Nobody hid it.

9
00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:16.900
It is the size.

10
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:27.370
Federal law said publish the negotiated rates, and they were, in machine files so big that opening one on a laptop is like drinking a reservoir through a straw.

11
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.100
The intent was daylight.

12
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:33.500
What arrived was a room with the lights on and nobody able to get in the door.

13
00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:34.980
We got through the door.

14
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.640
Five hundred and eight million rate rows, serving live.

15
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:47.040
Behind them, a drug rate lake of one point nine three billion rows that answers a question in one and seven tenths of a second.

16
00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.030
That is the sound of the file opening.

17
00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.970
Here is what is inside.

18
00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.910
One common procedure, in Sacramento.

19
00:00:54.730 --> 00:01:00.230
In a doctor's office, the negotiated rate is four hundred seventeen dollars and sixty five cents.

20
00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.430
In a surgery center, six hundred seventy nine dollars and ninety two cents.

21
00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:11.550
In a hospital outpatient department, one thousand one hundred nineteen dollars and fifty three cents.

22
00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:14.170
Same procedure, same city.

23
00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:24.520
Four hundred thirty nine dollars and sixty one cents between the surgery center and the hospital, decided by which building the patient sits down in.

24
00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:27.150
A new patient office visit, same city.

25
00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:29.900
Anthem files it at one hundred nine dollars.

26
00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:31.940
Blue Shield at four hundred three.

27
00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:33.070
Both published.

28
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:36.100
Neither on anybody's screen at renewal time.

29
00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.280
Now think about the meeting you had last spring.

30
00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.490
The employer leaned back and asked the honest question.

31
00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.030
Are we paying too much.

32
00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:47.260
And the honest answer available to anyone in that chair was a feeling.

33
00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:48.770
The market is tough this year.

34
00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:49.390
Everyone is up.

35
00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:51.970
That is what the closed file costs.

36
00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.000
Not a line item.

37
00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:56.090
A whole category of conversation you could not have.

38
00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.460
Sacramento is California's strongest data metro.

39
00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.260
Fifty one point four percent of peer cells are scoreable.

40
00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:04.730
Grade A.

41
00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.740
Your market is where this works best.

42
00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.630
You have sat through the other demos.

43
00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:16.590
Someone slid a confident figure across the table, you asked where it came from, and the room got vague.

44
00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:18.560
That is the problem.

45
00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:20.430
Not insurers.

46
00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.870
Opacity.

47
00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:25.250
A health plan pays for the room you are standing in.

48
00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:29.380
The enemy is that nobody will tell you how the number was made.

49
00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:30.880
So we tell you.

50
00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:34.250
And when we do not know, the screen says so.

51
00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:45.860
Ask for the standard office visit, code 99213, in Sacramento, and you get a refusal printed in plain sight: seventeen filings, and our publishing floor is one hundred.

52
00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:54.970
In the federal payment dispute record, San Francisco shows one thousand eight hundred seventy resolved lines at one point nine one times the benchmark.

53
00:02:55.790 --> 00:03:01.030
Sacramento gives you a refusal at four hundred thirty six, under the higher floor that record carries.

54
00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:09.010
Kaiser publishes no negotiated rate file at all, because it is a closed system, so we say that instead of inventing a number to fill the box.

55
00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:14.390
A tool that never says I do not know is lying to you somewhere, and you will not know where.

56
00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:16.510
Now here is the turn.

57
00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.760
Rates are what everyone expects.

58
00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:23.520
What changes your Monday is that the same discipline runs across your whole book.

59
00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:34.420
Every group you serve sits in one operator register, with the renewal clock counting down, so the ninety day window never arrives as a surprise in a carrier email.

60
00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:38.290
Beside each group, a dossier built from the public record.

61
00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:47.210
Eight thousand four hundred sixty seven California employer plan sponsors on the federal Form 5500.

62
00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:56.050
Three thousand two hundred seventy in the Bay Area and Sacramento corridors, three hundred forty eight in Sacramento itself.

63
00:03:56.380 --> 00:04:07.240
Nine hundred sixty eight million dollars of broker commission filed on California Schedule A for plan year 2023, across fifty two thousand two hundred sixty eight rows.

64
00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:13.170
That is your industry, describing itself, in public, all this time.

65
00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:21.520
Three hundred thirty six thousand three hundred twenty California provider affiliation rows, twenty two thousand two hundred twenty named groups.

66
00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:27.870
So who is actually in this network near our warehouse is an answer, not a project.

67
00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:29.310
Then the documents.

68
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:30.790
The rate exhibit.

69
00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.210
The market memo.

70
00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:33.940
The renewal brief.

71
00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.350
You do not hand over a screenshot.

72
00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:46.090
You hand over an exhibit with your firm's name on it, your language, the sources cited underneath, the refusals still printed where refusals belong.

73
00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:49.650
And the chief financial officer stops asking why it is going up.

74
00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:51.570
He starts asking what we do about it.

75
00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:52.690
That is a different meeting.

76
00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.850
That is a renewal you keep for five years.

77
00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:58.020
The automations keep watch while you sell.

78
00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:07.330
Thirteen codes retire on the thirtieth of September, inside renewal season, and you hear about it before the plan sponsor does.

79
00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:17.390
Eight thousand seven hundred sixty nine supply and equipment codes carry plain English names, so a wheelchair cushion reads like a wheelchair cushion.

80
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.120
And you can ask your own book a question in plain words.

81
00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.600
Which of my groups is exposed to that hospital rate.

82
00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:26.210
The answer comes back sourced.

83
00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.290
Your book stays in this browser.

84
00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.050
No patient information, no uploads, ever.

85
00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:36.750
One last figure, labelled the way the screen labels it.

86
00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:44.350
A two hundred fifty life California plan spends about three point nine five million dollars a year.

87
00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:56.520
That figure is modelled, from federal survey data, trended forward, with an honest range of fifteen thousand eight hundred to eighteen thousand five hundred dollars per employee.

88
00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:03.070
Mercer measured seventeen thousand four hundred ninety six in 2025.

89
00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:08.010
Modelled, not measured, and we say so in front of your client.

90
00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:14.650
In a market that sells confident numbers, the one willing to tell you no is the only one worth believing.

91
00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.740
Book a discovery call.

92
00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.050
Twenty minutes.

93
00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:24.110
Your metro, your codes, your groups, on the screen, with the refusals showing.

94
00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:27.161
Then walk into your next renewal holding the file.
